# Per-machine runtime state, never code.
#
# names/     the tab names you set with `nyan name`, keyed by tty
# spin-*.pid the running spinner daemons
# spin-*.lock the per-tty mutex, and the .stale.<pid> dirs a break renames aside
# branch-*   the 10-second git branch cache
#
# All of them are rebuilt on their own and are meaningless on another machine,
# because a tty number is not stable across reboots, let alone across hosts.

names/
spin-*.pid
spin-*.lock*
branch-*

# rate-limits: the status line's last usage reading, and what a killed write leaves.
# backup-*: local copies from before a hook change.
rate-limits*
backup-*/
